<title>SINGAPORE: SembCorp owns 54.8 pct S.Maritime.</title>
<headline>SembCorp owns 54.8 pct S.Maritime.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-11-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sembawang Corp Ltd owns 54.65 million shares or 54.8 percent of the issued share capital and Singapore $29.6 million or 85.4 percent of the convertible unsecured loanstock (CULS) of Sembawang Maritime Ltd after its voluntary offer expired on Friday.</p>
<p>The announcement was made by Standard Chartered Merchant Bank Asia Ltd on behalf of Farievo, SembCorp's wholly-owned vehicle for the take-over.</p>
<p>Before the voluntary offer on August 22, SembCorp and parties acting in concert owned 35.65 million shares or 35.8 percent of the issued share capital of SML and S$24.78 million or 71 percent of the CULS, which may be converted into 8.3 million new shares.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703080)</p>
